!
! Pythia8 cmd card for JetClass-I-style (v1) ZJetsToNuNu.
! This sample is MLM-matched (p p > ve ve~ j @0, p p > ve ve~ j j @1 - see
! mg5_step2_templ.dat/proc_card_mg5.dat), ickkw=1/xqcut=30 in run_card.
! JetMatching:qCut is meant to auto-fill from the LHE/MadGraph banner via
! JetMatching:setMad=on, but (like Main:numberOfEvents=-1 elsewhere) this
! Pythia8 build rejects -1 as out-of-range for qCut/nJetMax before setMad
! gets a chance to run, causing a hang. Set them explicitly instead:
! qCut matches run_card's xqcut=30.0. nJetMax is the TOTAL light-parton
! count of the highest-multiplicity sample (2, from the "j j" @1 process) -
! NOT the number of partons beyond the baseline (1) as a previous version
! of this comment/value assumed. JetMatching:exclusive defaults to 2
! (Pythia8Plugins/JetMatching.h/JetMatching.xml): per event, "nJet <
! nJetMax" -> exclusive matching, else inclusive - with nJetMax wrongly
! set to 1, the 2-parton ("code 1") sample had nJet(2) < nJetMax(1) always
! false, so it never got the inclusive-mode treatment a highest-multiplicity
! sample needs and was vetoed at a ~0% acceptance rate (verified directly:
! Pythia8's own "Number of events ... Accepted" breakdown by user
! classification code, generating from this gridpack standalone) - silently
! discarding the entire higher-particle-multiplicity population and
! explaining the resulting nparticles-per-jet deficit against central
! JetClass. With nJetMax=2, code-1 acceptance went from 0% to ~41% in the
! same test. See validation/compare-to-central-jetclass/ for the
! before/after comparison this was diagnosed from.
!
Main:numberOfEvents      = -1
HEPMCoutput:file         = events.hepmc
SysCalc:fullCutVariation = off
!
Random:setSeed = on
Random:seed = 0
!
Beams:frameType=4
JetMatching:merge=on
JetMatching:setMad=on
JetMatching:qCut=30.0
JetMatching:doShowerKt=off
JetMatching:nJetMax=2
HEPMCoutput:scaling=1.0000000000e+09
Check:epTolErr=1.0000000000e-02
!
LHEFInputs:nSubruns=1
Main:subrun=0
Beams:LHEF=unweighted_events.lhe.gz
